  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "WEEKNUM with an invalid return_type gave different answers in one build",
  "statement": "The documentation says an out-of-range return_type gives #NUM!. In recorded captures of one Excel build, 479 (serial_number, return_type) pairs were read with different results: usually #NUM!, sometimes a number (0, 1, 9, 10, 53 or 54). Some pairs differ within one run file. Every conflict has an invalid return_type (-5 to -1 or 22 to 129, 113 distinct values); no valid return_type conflicts. The conflict is open: no rule is claimed.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "The recorded readings conflict with each other; the counts come from the DnaCalc witness differences file.",
  "inferred": null,
  "documentation": {
    "claim": "If Return_type is out of the range specified in the table above, a #NUM! error is returned.",
    "source": "https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/office/weeknum-function-e5c43a03-b4ab-426c-b411-b18c13c75340"
  },
